  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "商業資訊系統",
    "sub_ename": "TRANSFORMING BUSINESS WITH INFORMATION SYSTEMS",
    "describe_ch": "本課程沒有任何先決條件。 當您上課時，強烈的課堂參與是非常重要的。 該課程將涵蓋硬件、軟件以及從當代 MIS 方面將信息通信技術 (ICT) 集成到課程基礎設施的核心部分。 將定期給予個人或小組團隊合作任務，學生的回應將有時間限制，以獲得學分。",
    "describe_eh": "There is no prerequisite for this course. Strong class participation is extremely essential while you attend the classes. The course will encompass hardware, software, and the integration of Information Communication Technology (ICT) into the core parts of the course infrastructure from the aspect of contemporary MIS. Individual or group teamwork assignments will be given periodically and the response from the students will be time limited in order to get the credits.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 3.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "本課程將完全用英語授課。 我強烈建議學生認為本課程是您從管理信息系統 (MIS) 的角度利用當代信息通信技術 (ICT) 為未來國際商務職業生涯的橋樑。 MIS 的成功應用已廣泛應用於許多業務領域，並以前所未有的速度繼續增長。 本課程的主要目的是為學生提供有關在不久的將來在商業應用領域中應用MIS的足夠背景知識。",
      "describe_en": "This course will be entirely taught in English. I strongly recommend the students to think that the course is the bridge for you to take advantage of contemporary Information Communication Technology (ICT) for future International Business career from Management Information System (MIS) point of view. The successful application of MIS has been widely applied in many business arena and it is continuing to grow in an unprecedented pace. The major objective of this course is to provide the students"
    }
  ],
